+<string id="he_pda_notes_module_name"><text>Route annotation module</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_notes_module_desc"><text>A memory board from a field navigator. Scraps of a paper route sketch and pencilled corrections remain on its casing. Its connector resembles a PDA connector, but it cannot be fitted directly. Vergas may be able to adapt it for custom map annotations.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_module_pickup"><text>A board from some kind of navigator. That connector looks familiar... Worth showing Vergas.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_module_ask"><text>Vergas, have a look at this. Could it fit a PDA?</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_module_lore"><text>I know these. Field navigators used them: survey an area, record the points, take the data away. See the paper on the casing? The previous owner was correcting a route by hand. Looks like he hoped to transplant the memory into another device. The connectors look alike, but the wiring differs. Plug it in blindly and you could burn out both boards.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_module_features_ask"><text>Could you adapt it?</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_module_offer"><text>I can. An adapter and a firmware adjustment will let you place and label your own map markers. It will not enlarge the battery or add a radiation meter. My fee is one first-tier artifact with at least half its condition remaining. You supply this board and a working PDA. I can do it while you wait.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_module_accept"><text>Agreed. Here are the board, PDA and artifact.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_module_wait"><text>Put them here. Keep your hands off the wires while I check it.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_module_finish"><text>All right. I will leave you to it.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_module_missing_ask"><text>What else do you need?</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_module_missing_answer"><text>This board, a working charged PDA, and a first-tier artifact with at least half its condition. I will not take a spent artifact. If someone is servicing your PDA, collect it first.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_sidor_strelok_ask"><text>You looked at the PDA I arrived with. What was on it?</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_sidor_strelok_answer"><text>One line stuck with me: "Kill Strelok." You could not tell me who you were, let alone who Strelok was. I do not sort out other people's orders, Marked One. Get back on your feet first. Then find out who wrote it.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_module_done"><text>Module installed. You can now place your own map annotations.</text></string>
